{"seq":2,"slug":"defi-protocols","title":"DeFi 协议经济学","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/cryptocurrency-blockchain-economics/defi-protocols","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"amm-liquidity-pool","title":"AMM 与流动性池机制","url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/cryptocurrency-blockchain-economics/defi-protocols/amm-liquidity-pool","wordCount":1686,"readingTime":7},{"seq":2,"slug":"lending-borrowing-protocols","title":"借贷协议经济模型","url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/cryptocurrency-blockchain-economics/defi-protocols/lending-borrowing-protocols","wordCount":1866,"readingTime":8},{"seq":3,"slug":"mev-transaction-ordering","title":"MEV 与交易排序经济学","url":"/l-doc-books/h/economics-finance/cryptocurrency-blockchain-economics/defi-protocols/mev-transaction-ordering","wordCount":1739,"readingTime":7}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"defi-协议经济学\">DeFi 协议经济学</h1><p>去中心化金融协议将传统金融的做市、借贷、交易排序等功能重构为链上可编程合约。这一章从经济学视角剖析三类核心协议：AMM 的流动性供给与无常损失、借贷协议的利率曲线与清算机制、以及 MEV 作为区块空间拍卖的经济后果。</p>\n<p>与技术实现不同，本章关注的是均衡条件、参与者激励和福利分配。AMM 流动性提供者面临的无常损失本质是期权卖方的 gamma 暴露；借贷协议的利率模型是利用率函数驱动的供需均衡；MEV 则揭示了区块生产中「谁排序，谁获益」的权力结构及其对用户福利的侵蚀。</p>\n"}